    "result_text": "All done. The change is implemented and the test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nReplaced the direct level-computation rule with a points system:\n\n**`util/MembershipPoints.java`** (new) \u2014 single responsibility: score an owner's points. Starts at 0, adds +2 (email), +1 (`namesakeCount == 0`), +2 (household of 3+ via `householdSize`), +3 (tenure > 365 days).\n\n**`util/MembershipLevel.java`** \u2014 now purely maps a points score to a level: 1 (0\u20131), 2 (2\u20133), 3 (4\u20135), 4 (6+). `of(owner)` delegates to `MembershipPoints` then `forPoints(...)`, so existing callers (`AuditOwnerCreated`) keep working unchanged.\n\n**`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 exposes both fields: added a `membershipPoints` mapping/helper alongside `membershipLevel`, each delegating to the util (no logic duplicated in the mapper).\n\n**`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `membershipPoints` schema property and updated `membershipLevel`'s description/range (now 1\u20134) so the generated `OwnerDto` carries both fields.\n\nThe tenure/points scoring stays factored into small units rather than piled into the mapper. `mvnw test` \u2192 `BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` (the acceptance test asserting `membershipPoints=3`, `membershipLevel=2` for a fresh owner with email and no namesake).",
