    "probe_text": "Here is the complete ordered sequence for `POST /api/owners`, as the code stands. The endpoint is defined in `src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml` as a single linear `next:` chain of 21 function steps. Every guard (steps 1\u201310) runs before any `Owner` object is built or persisted, so all rejections happen before mutation.\n\n## Gate (before any step)\n\n- **0. Authorization** \u2014 `composition.authorize: \"hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')\"`. No `OWNER_ADMIN` role \u2192 `AuthorizationDeniedException` \u2192 **403**.\n\n## Validations (steps 1\u201310, no owner persisted yet)\n\n1. **Required-field check** (`ValidateOwnerFields`) \u2014 first normalizes `address` in place (trim, collapse whitespace, upper-case, expand `ST/RD/AVE`), then requires `firstName, lastName, address, city, telephone` non-null and non-blank \u2192 else `MissingOwnerFieldsException` \u2192 **400**. Publishes the DTO for all later steps.\n2. **Telephone \u2192 E.164** (`NormalizeOwnerTelephone`) \u2014 converts to E.164 (defaults country `+61`, drops leading `0`, requires national-length match). Unparseable \u2192 `InvalidTelephoneException` \u2192 **400**. *Side-effect: mutates DTO telephone.*\n3. **Email format** (`NormalizeOwnerEmail`) \u2014 optional; if present must match email regex \u2192 else `InvalidEmailException` \u2192 **400**. *Side-effect: lower-cases/trims email on DTO.*\n4. **Disposable-email block** (`RejectDisposableEmail`) \u2014 rejects `mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com` \u2192 `DisposableEmailException` \u2192 **400**.\n5. **Postcode** (`ValidateOwnerPostcode`) \u2014 optional; must be exactly 4 digits and in-range for the city's region (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099; unknown cities accept any 4-digit) \u2192 else `InvalidPostcodeException` \u2192 **400**.\n6. **Registration date not future** (`ValidateRegistrationDate`) \u2014 optional; if supplied must not be after `LocalDate.now()` \u2192 else `FutureRegistrationDateException` \u2192 **400**.\n7. **Unique household identity** (`EnsureUniqueIdentity`, *transactional, reads all owners*) \u2014 unless `sharesHousehold=true` or no postcode, rejects if any existing owner shares the derived `householdId` \u2192 `DuplicateIdentityException` \u2192 **409**.\n8. **City capacity** (`EnsureCityCapacity`, *transactional, reads repo*) \u2014 rejects if the city already holds \u2265 50 owners \u2192 `CityCapacityExceededException` \u2192 **409**.\n9. **Resolve effective date** (`ResolveRegistrationDate`) \u2014 effective date = supplied else `now()`, rolled forward off weekends to Monday. Publishes `LocalDate`. (Not a rejection; a computation.)\n10. **Daily limit** (`EnsureDailyLimit`, *transactional, reads repo*) \u2014 rejects if \u2265 100 owners already carry the resolved date \u2192 `DailyLimitExceededException` \u2192 **429**.\n\n## Side-effects (steps 11\u201321, all inside `govern: [ transaction ]`)\n\n11. **Build owner** (`BuildOwner`) \u2014 MapStruct `OwnerMapper.toOwner(dto)` creates a new `Owner`; publishes it.\n12. **Apply registration date** (`ApplyRegistrationDate`) \u2014 stamps the resolved business-day date, overwriting whatever the body mapped.\n13. **Assign customer code** (`AssignCustomerCode`) \u2014 `customerCode = <REGION>-<HASH8>` (region from postcode/city; HASH8 = SHA-256 of telephone+lastName).\n14. **Assign membership number** (`AssignMembershipNumber`) \u2014 `membershipNumber = <customerCode>-M<YY>` (YY from adjusted registration year).\n15. **Assign household id** (`AssignHousehold`) \u2014 deterministic `householdId` (null if no postcode).\n16. **Assign household size** (`AssignHouseholdSize`, *reads repo*) \u2014 count of existing owners sharing the household id **+ 1**.\n17. **Count namesakes** (`AssignNamesakeCount`, *reads repo*) \u2014 count of existing owners with the same first+last name (case-insensitive).\n18. **Flag possible duplicate** (`AssignPossibleDuplicate`, *reads repo*) \u2014 unless `sharesHousehold=true`, sets `possibleDuplicate`/`possibleDuplicateOf` when an existing owner has same postcode + same lastName but a different telephone.\n19. **Persist** (`SaveOwner`, *reads/writes repo*) \u2014 `ownerRepository.save(owner)`; assigns the generated `id`. Hibernate re-validates the entity here (`@NotEmpty` on firstName/lastName/address/city/telephone, `@Pattern +[0-9]{8,15}` on telephone). A constraint failure \u2192 `DataIntegrityViolationException` \u2192 **409**.\n20. **Audit log** (`AuditOwnerCreated`) \u2014 writes an `AUDIT` logger line (id, customerCode, registrationDate, membershipLevel).\n21. **Respond** (`RespondWithOwnerCreated`) \u2014 maps to `OwnerDto` (computes displayName, initials, membership points/level, check digit, etc.), sets `bulkSignupWarning` (true when > 80 owners on the current business day), and returns **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}`.\n\n## Notes on the layering\n\n- The pipeline binds the body as a plain `@RequestBody` (no `@Valid` on the parameter), so the **hand-written checks in steps 1\u201310 are the effective create-time validation**, not the Bean Validation annotations on `OwnerFieldsDto`. Those annotations (`@Pattern` on names, `@Size` bounds, etc.) are the OpenAPI contract and only fire where framework validation applies (\u2192 `MethodArgumentNotValidException` \u2192 400).\n- The transaction boundary is not the whole pipeline: steps 7, 8, 10 and 11\u201321 are governed; step 9 sits ungoverned between them. Everything commits once at step 21.\n\nTwo things worth flagging as latent behavior rather than intent: the duplicate/capacity/namesake guards use `ownerRepository.findAll()` scans (O(n) per create), and the entity's telephone `@Pattern` is only satisfiable because step 2 normalizes to E.164 first \u2014 a change to either the normalizer or the pattern would surface as a 409 at save. Nothing was modified."
